OCMAT 1
# THE SAME MATERIAL AS M_PlainCube, PLUS ONE LINE. Every PARAM below matches that file exactly, so
# with the GRAPHREF removed this material renders indistinguishably from the control -- which is
# what makes the pair a proof rather than two unrelated surfaces.
#
# GRAPHREF names a `DOMAIN material` .ocgraph, content-relative. What it drives is BaseColor and
# Roughness; everything the graph does not drive -- metallic, the normal, emissive, occlusion,
# opacity -- still comes from the PARAM block below, which is the partial-graph behaviour the
# AverAuthored split in PbrShaders.cpp exists to provide. Change baseColorFactor here and the cube
# does NOT change, because the graph overwrote that field; change metallicFactor and it does.
SHADER standard
BLEND opaque
CULL back
FLAGS twosided=0 castshadow=1

PARAM baseColorFactor 0.55 0.55 0.58 1.0
PARAM metallicFactor 0.0
PARAM roughnessFactor 0.65
PARAM emissiveFactor 0.0 0.0 0.0
PARAM normalScale 1.0
PARAM occlusionStrength 1.0

GRAPHREF Materials/MG_Bands.ocgraph
